                  <items count="8">
                    <item name="Description" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">A panel for custom notes and text values</item>
                    <item name="InstanceGuid" type_name="gh_guid" type_code="9">66069d6c-1e63-49a5-bb56-d3c1beac472a</item>
                    <item name="Name" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">Panel</item>
                    <item name="NickName" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">Detailed description</item>
                    <item name="Optional" type_name="gh_bool" type_code="1">false</item>
                    <item name="ScrollRatio" type_name="gh_double" type_code="6">0</item>
                    <item name="SourceCount" type_name="gh_int32" type_code="3">0</item>
                    <item name="UserText" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">This file does one pretty simple thing, it puts an elipse on a line. There's a a lot of boilerplate, relatively, as the model itself is pretty simple.

This will change in the long run though, as this process is refined. The idea is that thse panels will become a different UI, and the python nodes that do the traversal and canvas screenshot will be less imposing.</item>
